Aim
To write and execute a Python program to load, clean and explore data using Pandas and NumPy libraries.
2. Algorithm
Start the program.
Import Pandas and NumPy libraries.
Create a dataset containing Team, Runs and Wickets.
Convert the dataset into a DataFrame.
Display the original data.
Check missing values using isna().sum().
Fill missing values with the mean using fillna().
Display the cleaned data.
Display the first five rows using head().
Display dataset information using info().
Display statistical summary using describe().
Display the shape of the dataset using shape.
Stop the program.
3. Source Code

import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

# 1. Load Data
data = {
    "Team": ["CSK", "MI", "RCB", "KKR", "CSK"],
    "Runs": [180, np.nan, 200, 175, 190],
    "Wickets": [5, 7, None, 6, 8]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print("Original Data:\n", df)

# 2. Check Missing Values
print("\nMissing Values:\n", df.isna().sum())

# 3. Clean Data
# Fill missing values with mean
df["Runs"] = df["Runs"].fillna(df["Runs"].mean())
df["Wickets"] = df["Wickets"].fillna(df["Wickets"].mean())

print("\nAfter Cleaning:\n", df)

# 4. Explore Data
print("\nFirst 5 Rows:\n", df.head())

print("\nInfo:")
df.info()

print("\nStatistical Summary:\n", df.describe())

print("\nShape (rows, columns):", df.shape)

